#5003
At the altar~
   You stand in a quiet room hung on all sides with black drapery, save
for the south wall, on which a stellar calendar has been painted in
silver and gold, full of symbols difficult to interpret.  Incense
smolders in a brass dish, and the hush is profound.  Reverence to the
elusive human deity is paid here.  The temple lies to the east, and
steps lead down to a silvery-lit landing.
