#5006
The temple garden~
   An impressionistic splash of red, black and gold meets the eye,
accompanied by the intoxicating fragrance of roses growing nearly wild
in this garden.  Their thorny canes have long since escaped their
trellises and now sprawl over the low stone walls and crumbling benches.
Bees drift lazily from bloom to bloom, and the walls of the temple
shelter the garden from the wind.  The sunken courtyard lies to the
west.
