#5019
At the gallows~
   In the shade of old, gnarl-limbed elder trees stands the bane of all
thieves and murderers: the platform of the gallows, its beam dark with
age.  The black sand of the road shows none of the blood that has been
shed here, but the legends of the dead live on in tales and nightmares.
Executions still take place at irregular intervals, to the joy of hidden
enemies and law-abiding citizens alike, and there is plenty of room for
spectators.  The road runs east and west, a path leads south, and steps
lead down to the stone arch.
~
